  "DescIdentified": {
    "type": "cexolocstring",
    "value": {
      "0": "The Basilisk King draped this coarse hide over his frame to ward off the biting frosts of the deep earth. It offers a formidable defense against the elements, though the heavy, lizard-like skin makes the mind turn inward and the senses dull.",
      "id": 67588
    }
  },
  "Description": {
    "type": "cexolocstring",
    "value": {
      "0": "Coarse, pebbled hide clings to the shoulders like a layer of dried mud. The skin retains a lingering, reptilian chill that numbs the skin beneath it."
    }
